# Line-ending and diff rules for a tree that carries binaries.
#
# Text is normalised to LF in the working tree on every platform. Without this
# a Windows checkout would rewrite every file, and `git diff` on a PNG would
# emit a textual patch.
#
# The binary rules matter here specifically: assets/ carries a 16MB CJK font,
# three .ogg recordings and PNG renders, and screenshots/ carries tracked
# captures. Left unclassified, git tries to diff them as text, and a merge
# conflict in a binary is unrecoverable -- the archive is unusable, not merely
# conflicted.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.c       text
*.h       text
*.mk      text
*.sh      text
*.py      text
*.mjs     text
*.md      text
*.json    text
*.yml     text
*.dsl     text
Makefile  text

*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.ogg     binary
*.otf     binary
*.ttf     binary
*.a       binary
